<title>USA: American Biogenetic gets FDA approval.</title>
<headline>American Biogenetic gets FDA approval.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON, Mass. 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Biogenetic Sciences Inc said on Wednesday that the Food and Drug Administration had granted marketing clearance for the company's fibrinogen test.</p>
<p>The test, known as the functional intact fibrinogen test, determines the quantity of fibrinogen in human plasma, which in turn provides a measurement of clotable protein levels in blood.</p>
<p>American Biogenetic, a biotechnology company, said it expects to launch the product during the fourth quarter of 1997.</p>
</text>
